---
/**
 * Privacy notice. Written to match what the code actually does (see functions/ and
 * migrations/). If the backend changes what it collects or how long it keeps it,
 * update this page in the same change.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const updated = "3 November 2026";
---

<Base
  locale="en"
  path="/privacy"
  localized={false}
  title="Privacy notice | TATVA"
  description="What personal data the TATVA website collects, why, how long it is kept, and how to see, correct or delete it."
>
  <article class="page container prose">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1>Your data, in plain words.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This notice explains what the TATVA website collects when you contact us or ask for help, why we need it, how
        long we keep it, and what you can ask us to do with it.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {site.legalName} ("TATVA", "we"), {site.location}, decides how the personal data described here is used. For
        any privacy question or request, contact {site.founder}:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
        <li>Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.phone.e164}`}>{site.phone.display}</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <p>We only collect what you choose to send us. Browsing the site does not require you to give us anything.</p>

      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">When you…</th><th scope="col">We receive</th><th scope="col">We use it to</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Send the project enquiry form</td>
              <td>Name, email, and, if you give them, phone, organisation, area of interest, budget range and your message</td>
              <td>Reply to your enquiry and discuss the work you asked about</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Ask a question or request help through the assistant</td>
              <td>Name, phone number, your area, what you need, any note you add, and whether you ask for yourself or for someone else</td>
              <td>Call you back and arrange the help you asked for</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Record a voice note</td>
              <td>The recording, its written transcript (which you can edit before sending), the language detected, your phone number and any note</td>
              <td>Understand your request and call you back</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Tap "Use my location"</td>
              <td>Your approximate position (latitude and longitude), only at that moment</td>
              <td>Find you, for example to deliver medicines or reach you for a visit</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Send anything through the site</td>
              <td>A one-way hash of your IP address (not the address itself) and the time</td>
              <td>Stop spam and abuse by limiting how often requests can be sent</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        Requests for TATVA Care may include health-related details such as medicines. Please share only what is needed
        to help you. TATVA Care is <strong>not an emergency service</strong>: in an emergency, call{" "}
        <a href="tel:112">112</a> or, for an ambulance, <a href="tel:108">108</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Consent</h2>
      <p>
        For voice notes and help requests, we ask for your consent before anything is sent. If you ask on behalf of
        someone else, such as a parent, please make sure they agree. You can withdraw consent at any time by
        contacting us (details above); we will then stop using your data for that request and delete it, unless the law
        requires us to keep it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who else handles your data</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your data or share it for advertising. We use these services to run the site:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the website, stores enquiries and requests in its database, and converts voice
          notes to text with its speech recognition service. If spam protection is switched on, Cloudflare Turnstile
          checks that a real person is sending the form.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Telegram</strong> delivers a copy of each enquiry or request, including any voice recording, to TATVA's
          private chat so that we can respond quickly.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>These providers may process data on servers outside India.</p>
      <p>
        Voice recordings are <strong>not stored in the website's database</strong>. They pass through the transcription
        service and are delivered to TATVA's private Telegram chat.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Project enquiries: deleted automatically 24 months after they are received.</li>
        <li>Assistant and TATVA Care requests: deleted automatically 12 months after they are received.</li>
        <li>Spam-prevention records (hashed IP address and time): deleted after 7 days.</li>
        <li>Copies delivered to TATVA's Telegram chat are deleted by us on the same schedule.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you ask us to delete your data sooner, we will, unless the law requires us to keep it.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>tell you what personal data we hold about you and how we use it;</li>
        <li>correct or complete it;</li>
        <li>delete it;</li>
        <li>withdraw a consent you gave;</li>
        <li>name another person to act for you if you cannot.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Send your request to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We will reply as soon as we can. If you
        are not satisfied with our response, you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies and preferences</h2>
      <p>
        The website does not use advertising or tracking cookies. It remembers your theme and sound choices
        in your own browser so that the site looks the way you left it; this stays on your device and is not sent to
        us.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The website is meant for adults. If you are under 18, please ask a parent or guardian to contact us for you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        All traffic to the site is encrypted. Only TATVA can see enquiries and requests. Access is limited to what is
        needed to respond to you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>If we change how we handle personal data, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <Footer locale="en" />
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + var(--s-16));
    padding-bottom: var(--s-24);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .head {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--s-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--text);
    max-width: 44ch;
  }
  .meta {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-12);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }
  p,
  li {
    color: var(--text);
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-2);
  }
  a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    min-width: 36rem;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  th {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 4%, transparent);
  }
  tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  td:first-child {
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-weight: 500;
    width: 24%;
  }
</style>
